  "type": "multiple-choice",
  "originalQuery": "You are in charge of a critical application that uses Cloud Spanner as its primary data store. There's an upcoming maintenance window during which you need to upgrade your schema. The application cannot afford more than 10 minutes of downtime. Which method should you employ to achieve this?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Apply schema updates directly as Cloud Spanner supports online schema updates without downtime.<br/>B. Conduct a hot backup of Cloud Spanner, perform the schema update, and restore the backup if needed.<br/>C. Use the Cloud Spanner Dataflow connector to replicate data, update the schema on the replica, and then switch traffic.<br/>D. Migrate data to a Cloud SQL instance, perform schema update, and migrate back to Cloud Spanner.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
